-- title:
--   Occurrence of a weight-two mod p eigensystem in J₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N$ a positive integer and $S$ a set of natural numbers, let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of the space of weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` at primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` at primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$ — to $F$. Regard [`ModularCurve.JZero N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L115), the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $N$ base-changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, as a module over [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlg`](def/HeckeGalois_EichlerShimura.html#L14) $= \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ via [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleBar`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L82), in which $X_\ell$ acts by the Hecke correspondence `heckeOperatorBar` at $\ell$. Then there is a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ such that: the constant $p$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}$; the residue field $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell]/\mathfrak{m}$ is finite; the submodule of elements of `JZero N` annihilated by every element of $\mathfrak{m}$ is non-zero; and there exist a field $F'$, a ring homomorphism $e : F \to F'$ and a ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell]/\mathfrak{m} \to F'$ with $\iota(X_\ell \bmod \mathfrak{m}) = e(\theta(T_\ell))$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$.
--
--   This is the occurrence statement of Deligne–Serre type in weight two: an arbitrary $F$-valued system of Hecke eigenvalues in characteristic $p$ is realised, after passage to a possibly larger field $F'$, by a non-zero $\mathfrak{m}$-torsion subgroup of the Jacobian of $X_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with $\mathfrak{m}$ of finite residue characteristic $p$. The extension $e$ is needed because an eigenform realising the system may have eigenvalues at the primes dividing $N$ or lying in $S$ that generate a field larger than the values of $\theta$; the statement feeds the weight-two construction of a Galois-stable line in [`GaloisRep.exists_conj_map_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_absolutelyIrreducible_of_eq_two`](thm.html#GaloisRep.exists_conj_map_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_absolutelyIrreducible_of_eq_two).
